      "item": "pthm-qft-example-regulated-probability-control",
      "finding": "The Statement defines projective measurements by self-adjoint idempotent, mutually orthogonal P_a summing to I, then says: “Equivalently, the one-Kraus-per-outcome data M_{a,1}=P_a form a normalized finite instrument”. The reverse implication is false without retaining the projection hypotheses. For example P₁=P₂=I/√2 gives a normalized one-Kraus-per-outcome instrument because P₁*P₁+P₂*P₂=I, but neither operator is idempotent. The cited finite-instrument definition requires only Kraus normalization. The subsequent proof uses the explicitly stated projection hypotheses, so this finding concerns the overstrong equivalence in the Statement.",
